1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,653
Every ambitious newcomer wants to tear

2
00:00:02,653 --> 00:00:04,539
down clunky old checklists,

3
00:00:04,539 --> 00:00:06,075
boring budget buffers,

4
00:00:06,075 --> 00:00:08,030
and legacy rules on day one.

5
00:00:08,030 --> 00:00:10,318
In his 1929 book The Thing,

6
00:00:10,318 --> 00:00:11,080
writer G.

7
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:11,419
K.

8
00:00:11,419 --> 00:00:14,639
Chesterton imagined a fence blocking a

9
00:00:14,639 --> 00:00:15,741
country road.

10
00:00:15,741 --> 00:00:17,774
Never tear down a fence,

11
00:00:17,774 --> 00:00:18,621
he warned,

12
00:00:18,621 --> 00:00:21,079
until you can state the exact

13
00:00:21,079 --> 00:00:23,790
reason someone paid to build it.

14
00:00:23,790 --> 00:00:26,666
Effective guardrails look pointless precisely because

15
00:00:26,666 --> 00:00:27,643
they work quietly.

16
00:00:27,643 --> 00:00:30,139
Deleting emergency cash reserves or pre-launch

17
00:00:30,139 --> 00:00:32,418
checks revives the forgotten disaster that

18
00:00:32,418 --> 00:00:33,720
originally created them.

19
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,746
Apply Chesterton's Audit before cutting any system:

20
00:00:36,746 --> 00:00:39,120
trace the failure that birthed the rule,

21
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:41,494
then verify whether that underlying risk

22
00:00:41,494 --> 00:00:42,740
actually disappeared.

23
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:44,800
Earn the right to simplify an

24
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:47,285
old guardrail by proving in writing

25
00:00:47,285 --> 00:00:49,771
that you understand what it quietly

26
00:00:49,771 --> 00:00:50,410
protects.
